WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:07.629
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Agents Of SHIELD did a little ABC crossover

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:10.440
and paid some fanservice to the Coulson May
shippers.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:16.800
It was really May’s episode but we learned
a lot more about their history together as

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.800
agents.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.230
Lots of stuff to get through so let’s start
with top 5 moments and then I’ll do my review.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:26.100
Also heads up, there was some major DC Justice
League Movie stuff that went down this morning

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:33.030
but I’m going to do a separate video about
that.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.000
Careful for spoilers in case you haven’t
seen the episode.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.140
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.430
Number 5 - Someone Else is writing Cosmic
Code all over the place

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.840
I think this is Skye’s Father.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.930
As far as we know, he’s one of the few other
crazy looking people who has knowledge of

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.490
the Obelisk.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:54.490
As for why he’s writing it on the back of
500 year old paintings of the Christ Child,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:01:00.070
we don’t know.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:14.729
The 
painting itself was a red herring, and now

00:01:14.729 --> 00:01:16.910
that coulson has it.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.380
I suspect it will just get lumped in with
Skye’s mission to decode the symbols.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:25.460
If you didn’t catch it, Coulson’s mental
breaks where he carves all over the wall.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.179
Those are coming more and more frequently.

00:01:27.179 --> 00:01:32.020
Eventually, he’ll just start spouting gibberish
about life, the universe and the meaning of

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.210
everything like Garret last season.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:38.299
That’s why he wants a contingency plan.

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:41.439
Number 4 - Dancing with the Stars

00:01:41.439 --> 00:01:47.530
Unless Dancing with the Stars does a cosplay
edition, I will never watch that show.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.600
But SHIELD did this cross promotion last night
where Clark Gregg and the other actors guest

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.600
starred on Dancing.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:56.049
Both tv shows air on ABC, so they’re just
promoting each other.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.670
It’s a business thing.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:13.340
In the SHIELD episode, the Dancing was just
an ode to classic secret agents stories.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:18.680
I don’t really enjoy those kinds of stories
anymore, so I felt like I was viewing the

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.430
whole thing from Skye’s perspective.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:26.310
She’s a good avatar for all the younger
viewers who look at this slow ballroom stuff

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.500
and go WTF is this.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.549
As a point of interest it was a lot of fun
to get the lazer focus on Coulson and May.

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:43.819
They brush over years of history together
with some witty jokes and suddenly it’s

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:45.090
fun for me again.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:50.290
I also got the sense behind the scenes, that
Clark Gregg and Ming Na the actors had a lot

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.549
of fun doing these dancing scenes.

00:02:52.549 --> 00:03:01.340
There is a lot of choreography that goes into
this.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.030
Number 3 - Clark Gregg Double O Seven

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:14.189
They make their move to get the painting and
in the process, make fun of 

00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:20.700
a lot of tropes from classic spy movies.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.140
Namely the gadgets.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.879
They probably could have just smashed their
way down to the basement and it would have

00:03:25.879 --> 00:03:26.879
been fine.

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:29.780
Like May said, they already knew they were
there.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.690
So who cares about the lazer grid.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.140
If it wasn’t clear during the Dancing, they’re
trying to make fun of spy movies.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:36.629
I really love the classic Bond Movies, but
let’s be honest, they’re totally hilarious

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:37.879
when you watch them now.

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:41.019
That’s why modern spy movies look more like
the Bourne Franchise.

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:45.849
The gadgets themselves do feel like they totally
fit inside the Stark Tech world of SHIELD.

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:48.489
I like the way the show balances it’s use
of gadgets.

00:03:48.489 --> 00:03:52.040
Number 2 - Doctor Whitehall Does His Own Dirty
Work

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.579
As far as TV Villains right now, I feel like
he’s one of the best, we haven’t really

00:03:56.579 --> 00:04:02.180
had enough time on Arrow or The Flash to get
to know those villains, so I’m interested

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:08.239
to see who the worst is at the end of everyone’s
season.

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:11.130
Like will SHIELD have a better TV Villain
than the other shows.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:16.079
I might be having more fun with the character
just because I’m familiar with his work

00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:20.570
inside the Whedonverse on Dollhouse and Much
Ado About Nothing.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:28.100
It feels like he’s tailor made for this
very calm collected evil nazi person.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.090
That speech he gave Raina too, that was good.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:36.060
He threatened that he’d torture her for
a couple weeks with unnecessary surgery without

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.530
letting her pass out.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:42.310
If you ever watch other science fiction stories
that do things like this.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:48.229
Sometimes you’ll see the villains talk about
activating different pain centers in the brain

00:04:48.229 --> 00:04:55.200
so that your body doesn’t have the chance
to adapt and it ends up being a much more

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.200
painful process.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.460
Very terrifying, very good performance.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.900
He’s setting the bar for Ra’s Al Ghul
on Arrow.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.530
and my Number 1 - Face Off May

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:07.020
This really was her episode.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.180
Coulson and everyone else were just guest
stars.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.770
I love the way they humanize these crazy situations
with little character bits like “May Hates

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.130
Coffee”, or letting Clark Gregg Punch Ming
Na in the Face.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.050
That was just some great special effects work.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:22.190
Yes the gadgets are ridiculous, but in the
context of this episode, they totally worked

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:23.530
for me.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:37.680
May’s fight scene was also probably my favorite
of any tv fight scene this year.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:43.460
Arrow has amazing fight choreography, but
this was a gloves off moment for the Cavalry.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:51.080
If it were legal to post clips of tv shows
I would just make montages of her fight scenes.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:55.250
I could make an entire youtube channel that’s
just AMV Fight Scenes.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:06:00.389
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and do you think Raina will hand over the

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:01.389
Obelisk?

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:06.009
I kind of hoped she’d manifest some crazy
power and blow the car up.

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:07.560
There weren’t a lot of easter eggs I noticed
so I’m just going to head straight to my

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:08.560
review.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:09.560
If you did see any big ones just write them
in the comments.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:13.110
Overall I gave the episode a B plus for doing
such great character work with May and Coulson,

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.840
while at the same time, making fun of all
the cheesy spy movies.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.229
It was like a nice Whedonverse Cheese Spread.

00:06:19.229 --> 00:06:22.919
I could have done without the dancing, but
it didn’t take me out of the episode too

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:23.919
much.

00:06:23.919 --> 00:06:27.660
It felt a little like an episode I would show
to my parents if I wanted to get them to watch

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:28.720
SHIELD.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.060
They grew up with all these cheesy spy movies,
and Dancing with the Stars has a much older

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:35.069
Demo than the comic book shows.

00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:40.850
So you can see how Dancing with Agents of
SHIELD is a bit of a hat tip to older viewers.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:46.289
I totally love cheesy things in my tv shows,
Gotham is a good example of a cheesy comic

00:06:46.289 --> 00:06:48.330
book show that I totally love.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:52.370
So Whedonverse cheese is always appreciated.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:57.240
Ming Na just keeps on proving why she’s
the biggest badass female on tv right now.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.160
Let me know of all the big female characters
on tv right now who do you think is the most

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.160
badass.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:01.160
Just pick from any of your favorite shows.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:05.110
We’ll make them fight Agent May to the death
during sweeps week.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.490
Next week the big news is Adrianne Palicki
is debuting as Mockingbird from the comics.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:12.740
The title of the episode is A Hen in the Wolfhouse.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.669
If you saw the promo, it’s of her inside
a HYDRA base.

00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:18.129
The title is a play on the saying A Wolf in
the Henhouse.

00:07:18.129 --> 00:07:21.300
It just means that she is a SHIELD double
agent like Simmons.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.870
So she will be beating the crap out a lot
of HYDRA people.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:29.530
I’ll probably post that video next Wednesday
morning.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.220
So be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:41.460
and like I said, a ton of DC Movies after
Justice League got announced, Jason Momoa

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:46.289
Aquaman, a new Green Lantern Movie, a Flash
movie, it’s crazy.

00:07:46.289 --> 00:07:48.979
So I’ll talk more about that in my Arrow
video tonight.

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:52.620
And just to follow up on robert downey jr
in captain america.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:57.360
for those wondering, Marvel typically doesn’t
comment when big stories like this leak out.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.180
But the original story and the 40 million
dollar payday were reported by Variety and

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:06.270
they are one of the more trusted news sources
out there.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:09.789
So you should believe that at this moment,
this is what’s happening.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:15.650
The movie isn’t getting made for a while,
so there’s always the chance details could

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:16.650
change.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:19.949
In which case I’ll post more updates.

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:25.879
Right now click here to learn more about what’s
going on with that and click here for my SHIELD

00:08:25.879 --> 00:08:26.879
episode 3 video.

00:08:26.879 --> 00:08:29.430
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and meet back up for Arrow tonight!

